WEBVTT

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.960
I want to welcome Harry and his daughter Michelle

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.720
to Thanksgiving with us.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.020
Thank you, Dr. Stewart.

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:14.360
But first, I think we should take a moment

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.560
and remember the meaning of Thanksgiving.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.700
Philip, I took Michelle to a school play

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:20.740
about the first Thanksgiving.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.160
Well, why don't you tell us about that, Michelle?

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:25.740
Thanksgiving was about the Pilgrims,

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.360
the first settlers in America.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:29.540
They shared the first harvest with the Indians

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:36.160
Then in that spirit let each of us give thanks.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.240
Each in his own way.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.040
Who wants to begin?

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:40.340
I will.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:45.880
I give thanks for being here with my family and for being well,

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:47.960
so I can enjoy you all.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.660
We love you, Grandpa.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:57.980
I'd like to give thanks for a healthy year, a good job,

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.860
and for meeting Harry and Michelle.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.480
We'd like to give thanks for meeting Susan

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.280
and the Stewart family.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:08.140
Thanks, Harry.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:09.640
That was very kind of you.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.800
I'd like to give thanks for Grandpa coming to live with us.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.560
And I'd also like to thank my math teacher

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.380
for giving me a passing grade.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:26.320
You go first, Marilyn.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:27.920
I'm thinking.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:28.860
You go first.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:34.600
Well, you all know I'm working on my photo album.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:36.780
It's not finished yet.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:40.080
And I'd like to thank Marilyn for being so patient.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.480
Thanks, Richard.

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:45.080
I should thank you for encouraging me

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.640
to keep working on my fashion designs.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:50.120
I'm lucky to have a husband with an artistic eye.

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:56.340
Oh, we have a lot to be thankful for.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.720
For the food on this table.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.200
Just like the Pilgrims.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:02.320
I'll go along with that, Ellen.

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:04.900
Well, help me serve, Robbie.

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:10.380
It was a wonderful meal, Mrs. Stewart.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:10.880
Thank you.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.140
And now to see the end of the football game.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:13.820
Exactly.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.080
Where are you going, Philip?

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:18.600
Remember, the Michigan football game?

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.440
And Michigan needs a touchdown.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:22.360
Did you forget something?

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:25.100
Dad, your famous apple pie.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:27.600
Just let me see the score, Ellen.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:29.200
Go ahead, Philip.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.170
We should all take a little break before dessert.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.390
Oh, who could that be?

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:47.240
Oh, it must be Alexandra.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:50.120
I invited her to come by for dessert.

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:50.820
You did?

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:52.540
I like Ellen.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.020
You know everyone, Alexandra.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:57.420
No, she doesn't know Harry Bennett and his daughter Michelle.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:58.740
Nice to meet you.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:02:59.260
Hi.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:00.880
Hello, Alexandra.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:03.120
Hi, Susan.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:03.820
Happy Thanksgiving.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.820
And Alexandra brought us a pumpkin pie.

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.060
Please sit down, Alexandra.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:11.820
Dad, Richard--Alexandra's here.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:14.960
Michigan needs a touchdown.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:16.040
Three minutes to play.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:17.520
Hi, Alexandra. Welcome.

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:18.820
Hello, Alexandra.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:20.560
Yes, Michigan needs a touchdown.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:24.020
One tiny little touchdown, with just three minutes to play.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:25.600
You want Michigan to win.

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:29.840
And Alexandra brought us a pumpkin pie.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:42.580
What happened?

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.560
We forgot to turn the oven on.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.400
We did?

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.280
Philip, why don't you go

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:53.300
watch the last three minutes of the game.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:56.140
I will serve coffee and pumpkin pie.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:58.900
OK. I'll be back in a few minutes.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:03.040
Robbie, would you bring the dessert plates.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:04.760
And, Marilyn, would you pour coffee, please.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:05.360
Sure, Ellen.

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:11.570
How was your Thanksgiving dinner, Alexandra?

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:13.720
Just wonderful, Mr. Stewart.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.900
The Molinas are a large family.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:17.250
I love being with them.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:19.200
I'm glad you came by, Alexandra.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:20.200
I am, too.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:27.440
Touchdown! Touchdown! Touchdown!

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:33.020
Lots to be thankful for.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:35.240
Michigan scored a touchdown.

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:37.680
Alexandra came by.

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:41.580
And nobody misses Philip's famous apple pie.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:43.520
Oh, Grandpa!
